4.2 step 5).    |\n  1295\t| P1 wait entry incomplete         | Agreed. `:link-request` and         |\n  1296\t|                                  | `:link-response`; cursor minted     |\n  1297\t|                                  | before append; envelope and both    |\n  1298\t|                                  | descriptors retained (7.2 steps 3-4)|\n  1299\t| P1 correlation unspecified       | Agreed. Exact id match; per-entry   |\n  1300\t|                                  | kept cursor advancing past others;  |\n  1301\t|                                  | duplicate, late, unknown, abandoned |\n  1302\t|                                  | fixed (7.2 step 7). Divergence:     |\n  1303\t|                                  | per-entry cells rather than one     |\n  1304\t|                                  | router cursor, so a parked entry    |\n  1305\t|                                  | stays a UCF cell and migrates.      |\n  1306\t| P1 install cannot be synchronous | Agreed; r1's claim withdrawn.       |\n  1307\t|                                  | Scheduler child task with phases,   |\n  1308\t|                                  | own store and wait-set, waiter set, |\n  1309\t|                                  | `:install` wait reason (7.3).       |\n  1310\t| P1 four-way pairing unverified   | Agreed. `:yin.module/tree` plus one |\n  1311\t|                                  | `derive-record` per format;         |\n  1312\t|                                  | input/output checked; verifying or  |\n  1313\t|                                  | trusted, named; swapped-image tests |\n  1314\t|                                  | for all formats (8.1, M4).          |\n  1315\t| P1 manifest name unchecked       | Agreed. `:module-name-mismatch`     |\n  1316\t|                                  | after manifest validation (8.1).    |\n  1317\t| P1 authority open at M4          | Agreed. Fail-closed assertion       |\n  1318\t|                                  | policy with asserter, snapshot,     |\n  1319\t|                                  | retraction, `:ambiguous-name`; M4   |\n  1320\t|                                  | entry criterion (8.2, M4).          |\n  1321\t|                                  | Authentication of principals stays  |\n  1322\t|                                  | open and is named as such (12).     |\n  1323\t| P2 decoupling not strict         | Agreed as stated: strict decoupling |\n  1324\t|                                  | is H/R only, said plainly (3); the  |\n  1325\t|                                  | pinning amendment is recorded as a  |\n  1326\t|                                  | UCF / code-as-tuples decision (12). |\n  1327\t| P2 unary segment-key at step 3   | Agreed. `segment-matches?` for the  |\n  1328\t|                                  | storage-derived formats (4.1, 5).   |\n  1329\t| P2 unbounded parts               | Agreed. `:row-defect-fn` before     |\n  1330\t|                                  | enqueue; `:max-parts`, `:max-depth`,|\n  1331\t|                                  | `:max-bytes`; `:parts-limit` (4.2). |\n  1332\t| P2 fetch's handle is a backdoor  | Agreed. `fetch` takes a link        |\n  1333\t|                                  | runtime with a driver; no handle;   |\n  1334\t|                                  | traffic-equivalence test (6.4, M3). |\n  1335\t| P2 DHT is not a stream endpoint  | Agreed. DHT handle behind           |\n  1336\t|                                  | `serve-content!`; equivalence       |\n  1337\t|                                  | claimed at the linker boundary only;|\n  1338\t|                                  | stepped client out of scope (6.1).  |\n  1339\t| P2 host modules unconstrained    | Agreed. Profile classes enforced at |\n  1340\t|                                  | registration; `:host` refused;      |\n  1341\t|                                  | effectful exports return effect     |\n  1342\t|                        