{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '239,546p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | nl -ba -v 239\"","aggregated_output":"   239\t## 4. The fetch pipeline\n   240\t\n   241\t### 4.1 The format record\n   242\t\n   243\tA format record is a plain map held in linker-local state. B6 fixed three\n   244\tfunction slots; this revision replaces one, renames one, and adds three:\n   245\t\n   246\t```clojure\n   247\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.code      ; the dispatch key\n   248\t :contract            \"b1\"                    ; contract revision name\n   249\t :identity-fn         (fn [value] identity)   ; mint: publish! only\n   250\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [identity value] boolean) ; step 3\n   251\t :row-defect-fn       (fn [value] defect-or-nil)    ; step 2, per part\n   252\t :validate-fn         (fn [value] defect-or-nil)    ; step 4, whole\n   253\t :obligations-fn      (fn [value] [sym ...])        ; step 5a input\n   254\t :parts-fn            (fn [value] [address ...])}   ; step 2 worklist\n   255\t```\n   256\t\n   257\t- `:identity-fn` mints an identity from a payload. It is used by\n   258\t  `publish!` and never by verification.\n   259\t- `:identity-matches-fn` is the step-3 check, directed by the identity.\n   260\t  For H and R it is `(= identity (image-hash value))`, a contract-pinned\n   261\t  hash with one algorithm. For the storage-derived formats it is\n   262\t  `(jing/segment-matches? identity value)`, so a value minted under\n   263\t  `:sha256` while the default is `:blake3` verifies under the algorithm\n   264\t  the identity names and never fails spuriously.\n   265\t- `:row-defect-fn` validates one fetched part on its own, before any\n   266\t  address it references is enqueued: tag, arity, slot kinds, saturation.\n   267\t  For single-payload formats it is the whole validator, run early.\n   268\t- `:parts-fn` returns the storage addresses a fetched payload references\n   269\t  and without which it is incomplete. For the three single-payload\n   270\t  formats it returns nothing. For `:yin.ast/code` it returns the child\n   271\t  row ids of a row body.\n   272\t- `:obligations-fn` returns the free names of a value. The linker joins\n   273\t  them with the manifest's declarations to form obligations (step 5a).\n   274\t\n   275\t`fetch` and `step` contain no branch on `:format`. Adding a fifth backend\n   276\tis one more record.\n   277\t\n   278\t### 4.2 The six steps\n   279\t\n   280\tThe order is B6's, unchanged, and remains load-bearing for the reasons\n   281\tB6 gives. Step 2 is a bounded worklist; steps 1 and 2 are stream\n   282\texchanges (section 6); step 5 has a linker half and a receiver half.\n   283\t\n   284\t```text\n   285\t(link runtime format identity)\n   286\t\n   287\t1. address    <- (index identity)               linker-local index\n   288\t                 absent entry                       -> :absent\n   289\t2. payload    <- fetch address over dao.stream\n   290\t                 absent payload                     -> :absent\n   291\t                 (not (segment-matches? address v)) -> :address-mismatch\n   292\t                 ((:row-defect-fn format) v)        -> :descriptor-defect\n   293\t                 bounds exceeded                    -> :parts-limit\n   294\t                 enqueue ((:parts-fn format) v); repeat until empty\n   295\t3.               (not ((:identity-matches-fn format) identity root))\n   296\t                                                    -> :hash-mismatch\n   297\t4.               ((:validate-fn format) whole) returns a defect\n   298\t                                                    -> :descriptor-defect\n   299\t                 request contract differs from record's\n   300\t                                                    -> :contract-mismatch\n   301\t5a.              obligations <- join free names with declarations\n   302\t                 free name with no declaration      -> :undeclared-free\n   303\t5b.  (receiver)  each obligation discharged by exact equality\n   304\t                 profile or manifest differs        -> :unresolved-free\n   305\t                 name bound in free env or store    -> :shadowed-free\n   306\t6. return the verified image as data\n   307\t```\n   308\t\n   309\tStep by step, for all four formats:\n   310\t\n   311\t1. **Resolve identity to storage address.** The index is linker-local\n   312\t   composition data: a map, or datoms `[identity attribute address]`\n   313\t   read through `index-from-datoms` from a `dao.space` source the linker\n   314\t   observes with its own cursor. An entry that has not been observed\n   315\t   yet is `:absent` now, which is the honest answer at this moment; a\n   316\t   later request may find it. Step 1 never waits and never queries a\n   317\t   remote index inline. For the storage-derived formats the identity is\n   318\t   its own address and the index is the identity function.\n   319\t2. **Fetch payload over `dao.stream`.** Each address is a\n   320\t   `:jing/get-content` request on the content request stream and a\n   321\t   correlated response on the content response stream (section 6). The\n   322\t   value is verified against the address it was requested at, using the\n   323\t   algorithm the address carries (`jing/segment-matches?`). Then, before\n   324\t   any child is enqueued, `:row-defect-fn` validates this part alone;\n   325\t   a malformed row is refused here and its slots are never followed.\n   326\t   Then `:parts-fn` names further addresses; each is fetched and\n   327\t   verified the same way; the worklist is breadth-first from the root\n   328\t   and visits each address once. The composition supplies bounds in the\n   329\t   runtime: `:max-parts`, `:max-depth`, `:max-bytes`; exceeding any is\n   330\t   `:parts-limit` naming the bound and the address at which it was hit.\n   331\t   The result of step 2 is the root value plus, for a multi-part\n   332\t   format, the map of every fetched part by address.\n   333\t3. **Verify format identity.** `(:identity-matches-fn format)` over the\n   334\t   requested identity and the root value. For H and R this is a\n   335\t   different hash under a different preimage from step 2 and catches a\n   336\t   stale or swapped index entry, a descriptor disagreement, or a\n   337\t   contract version disagreement (all `:hash-mismatch`, as in B6). For\n   338\t   the storage-derived formats it is `segment-matches?` under the\n   339\t   identity's own algorithm; it still runs, because it is the only check\n   340\t   that the *index* did not point the identity at a different, correctly\n   341\t   stored payload.\n   342\t4. **Validate structural and liveness invariants.** The format's\n   343\t   validator runs over the complete value: for a tree, over the\n   344\t   assembled row set (`:id-resolves`, `:acyclic`, `:root-reachable` are\n   345\t   whole-tree rules that step 2's row-local check cannot run); for a\n   346\t   vector, over the vector; for a register image, including the\n   347\t   ascending, bounded, exact live-set rules. A validator that throws is\n   348\t   `:descriptor-defect` with rule `:validator-refused`. If the request\n   349\t   named a contract revision and the format record's `:contract`\n   350\t   differs, the refusal is `:contract-mismatch`, raised before any\n   351\t   grammar check that would run under the wrong table.\n   352\t5. **Verify dependency closure.** Two halves.\n   353\t   - *5a, at the linker: obligations.* `:obligations-fn` yields the free\n   354\t     names. Each is joined with the manifest that delivered the image\n   355\t     (section 8.1): a name under `:yin.module/primitives` becomes\n   356\t     `{:name n :kind :primitive :profile addr}`; a name exported by a\n   357\t     module under `:yin.module/requires` becomes\n   358\t     `{:name n :kind :module :module m :manifest addr}`. A free name\n   359\t     the manifest declares nowhere is `:undeclared-free`; the publisher\n   360\t     did not say what the name means, so no receiver can bind it\n   361\t     identically. An image requested by bare identity with no manifest\n   362\t     has no declarations; it verifies only if it has no free names,\n   363\t     which is B6's closed-image case and remains supported.\n   364\t   - *5b, at the receiver: discharge.* Obligations travel with the\n   365\t     verified image in the response. The receiver checks each against\n   366\t     its live state as the first act of installation, before any load:\n   367\t     a `:primitive` obligation is discharged only by a primitive of\n   368\t     equal profile address; a `:module` obligation only by a linked\n   369\t     module of equal manifest address; a name bound in the receiver's\n   370\t     free env or store is `:shadowed-free`; anything else is\n   371\t     `:unresolved-free` naming the obligation and what was found. This\n   372\t     is UCF section 7.5.2's rule (\"checked by profile, not by presence\")\n   373\t     at the linker's grain, and D11's refusal for an image the receiver\n   374\t     cannot bind identically.\n   375\t   Discharge is at the receiver because the receiver's store and free\n   376\t   env are live state; a snapshot sent on the wire is stale by\n   377\t   construction and would license a binding that no longer holds. The\n   378\t   host-policy `fetch` (section 6.4), which runs in one process with the\n   379\t   receiver in hand, runs both halves before returning.\n   380\t6. **Return the verified image.** `{:status :ok :format f :identity i\n   381\t   :address a :value v :obligations [...]}` plus `:parts {address value}`\n   382\t   for a multi-part format and `:derivation {...}` where a manifest\n   383\t   supplied one (section 8.1). Nothing partially verified is ever\n   384\t   returned.\n   385\t\n   386\t### 4.3 Refusal vocabulary\n   387\t\n   388\tEvery refusal is `{:status :refused :reason r}` merged with the step's own\n   389\tevidence, exactly as `yin.vm.linker/refused` builds it.\n   390\t\n   391\t| Reason                  | Step   | Meaning                                  |\n   392\t|-------------------------|--------|------------------------------------------|\n   393\t| `:absent`               | 1 or 2 | no index entry, or no payload at the     |\n   394\t|                         |        | address (root or any part)               |\n   395\t| `:address-mismatch`     | 2      | payload does not hash to its address     |\n   396\t| `:parts-limit`          | 2      | a composition bound on parts, depth, or  |\n   397\t|                         |        | bytes was exceeded                       |\n   398\t| `:hash-mismatch`        | 3      | root value does not match the identity   |\n   399\t| `:descriptor-defect`    | 2 or 4 | row-local or whole-value validation      |\n   400\t|                         |        | failed                                   |\n   401\t| `:contract-mismatch`    | 4      | request names a contract the format      |\n   402\t|                         |        | record does not implement                |\n   403\t| `:undeclared-free`      | 5a     | a free name has no declaration in the    |\n   404\t|                         |        | manifest that delivered the image        |\n   405\t| `:unresolved-free`      | 5b     | an obligation is not discharged by an    |\n   406\t|                         |        | equal profile or manifest                |\n   407\t| `:shadowed-free`        | 5b     | an obligation's name is bound by the     |\n   408\t|                         |        | receiver's free env or store             |\n   409\t| `:unsupported-format`   | before | the receiver holds no kernel or format   |\n   410\t|                         | 1      | record for the requested format          |\n   411\t| `:module-name-mismatch` | 8.1    | the manifest declares a name other than  |\n   412\t|                         |        | the one it was resolved under            |\n   413\t| `:ambiguous-name`       | 8.2    | more than one accepted assertion for a   |\n   414\t|                         |        | name at the snapshot                     |\n   415\t| `:derivation-mismatch`  | 8.1    | an image's derivation record does not    |\n   416\t|                         |        | lead from the manifest's tree, or a      |\n   417\t|                         |        | verifying re-lowering disagrees          |\n   418\t| `:export-missing`       | 7.3    | the evaluated module did not bind an     |\n   419\t|                         |        | export the manifest names                |\n   420\t| `:require-cycle`        | 7.4    | a child install requires a module that   |\n   421\t|                         |        | is itself installing in its ancestry     |\n   422\t| `:pairing-mismatch`     | verify | B6's same-root check (now a case of      |\n   423\t|                         |        | `:derivation-mismatch`, kept by name)    |\n   424\t\n   425\t`:unsupported-format` is the linker's instance of the host-boundary rule\n   426\tthat a host with no implementation for an effect emits a qualified\n   427\tunsupported result, \"a correct outcome, not a gap to be filled\"\n   428\t(`datom.world.md`). It lets a receiver decline an R request and, where\n   429\tthe composition permits, fall back to H by the manifest's derivations.\n   430\t\n   431\tA stepped link additionally reports `:pending` (section 6.3), which is\n   432\tnot a refusal: it is the \"not yet\" of a non-blocking read.\n   433\t\n   434\t## 5. Format records for the four backends\n   435\t\n   436\tThree records bind existing code; the AST record's free-name scanner is\n   437\tthe section 4.5 query of `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md`, implemented as\n   438\t`yin.vm/free-names`.\n   439\t\n   440\t### 5.1 `:yin.ast/code` (the AST walker)\n   441\t\n   442\t```clojure\n   443\t{:format              :yin.ast/code\n   444\t :contract            \"v2\"\n   445\t :identity-fn         (fn [body] (jing/segment-key body))\n   446\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [root-id body] (jing/segment-matches? root-id\n   447\t                                                                  body))\n   448\t :row-defect-fn       (fn [body] (row-local-defect body))\n   449\t :validate-fn         (fn [tree] (yin.vm/validate-rows tree))\n   450\t :obligations-fn      (fn [tree] (yin.vm/free-names (relation tree)\n   451\t                                                    (occurrences tree)\n   452\t                                                    (:root tree)))\n   453\t :parts-fn            (fn [body] (body-child-ids body))}\n   454\t```\n   455\t\n   456\tPayload: one row body `[tag & slots]` per address, exactly as\n   457\t`yin.vm.content/materialize-tree!` stores it (D3: individual rows, no pack\n   458\tformat; the body is what is hashed, and the id is derived from it). The\n   459\tidentity is the root row's id. Steps 2 and 3 therefore hash the fetched\n   460\tbody as received; the address is prepended only when the linker assembles\n   461\t`{id [id tag & slots]}` for step 4, the shape `validate-rows` takes.\n   462\t`row-local-defect` runs the `:tag`, `:arity`, `:slot-kind`, and\n   463\t`:saturation` rules of section 7.4 over one body, so a malformed row\n   464\tnever has its slots followed. Step 2's worklist follows `node` and\n   465\t`nodes` slots by the grammar's positions, the walk\n   466\t`yin.vm.content/load-rows` performs today; that function's throwing\n   467\tsurface is retired in favor of the linker's refusals (section 9).\n   468\tFree names are the conservative, occurrence-scoped set. Loading is\n   469\t`yin.vm.ast-walker/vm-load-rows`.\n   470\t\n   471\t### 5.2 `:yin.semantic/code` (the semantic VM)\n   472\t\n   473\t```clojure\n   474\t{:format              :yin.semantic/code\n   475\t :contract            \"v2\"\n   476\t :identity-fn         jing/segment-key\n   477\t :identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?\n   478\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.code/well-formed-vector?\n   479\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.code/well-formed-vector?\n   480\t :obligations-fn      semantic-free-names\n   481\t :parts-fn            (constantly nil)}\n   482\t```\n   483\t\n   484\tPayload: the canonical positional instruction tuple vector (UCF section\n   485\t7.3.2), stored as the exact vector at its own `segment-key`; nothing\n   486\telse may hash there (UCF section 7.3.4). The identity is that address.\n   487\t`well-formed-vector?` is the section 7.5 grammar. `semantic-free-names`\n   488\tscans `:var` operands not bound by an enclosing closure's params, the\n   489\t`$code` query of section 7.7; the linker module defines it, as B6\n   490\tdefined the two de Bruijn scanners. The contract stamp is UCF's\n   491\t`{:yin.code/contract \"v2\"}`; a link request for this format carries the\n   492\tstamp, and the receiver's index is keyed per stamp (UCF section 7.3.3).\n   493\tLoading is `yin.vm.semantic/load-vector`, which writes the address to the\n   494\timage and the alias column.\n   495\t\n   496\t### 5.3 `:yin.debruijn.code` (the stack VM)\n   497\t\n   498\t```clojure\n   499\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.code\n   500\t :contract            \"b1\"\n   501\t :identity-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash\n   502\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [H v] (= H (yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-hash v)))\n   503\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect\n   504\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-code/image-defect\n   505\t :obligations-fn      stack-free-names\n   506\t :parts-fn            (constantly nil)}\n   507\t```\n   508\t\n   509\tUnchanged from B6 section 5.1 in substance. The identity H is\n   510\t`image-hash` over the descriptor hash (which embeds the lowering contract\n   511\tversion) and the canonical vector; the `=` here compares two values of\n   512\tone contract-pinned hash and is not a Class 3 site. Free names are\n   513\t`:load-free` operands. Loading is `yin.vm.debruijn.stack/load-image`;\n   514\t`yin.repl`'s `append-stack-image` shows the relocation a second image\n   515\tneeds beside a held one.\n   516\t\n   517\t### 5.4 `:yin.debruijn.register` (the register VM)\n   518\t\n   519\t```clojure\n   520\t{:format              :yin.debruijn.register\n   521\t :contract            \"r1\"\n   522\t :identity-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash\n   523\t :identity-matches-fn (fn [R v]\n   524\t                        (= R (yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-hash\n   525\t                               v)))\n   526\t :row-defect-fn       yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-image-defect\n   527\t :validate-fn         yin.vm.debruijn-register-code/register-image-defect\n   528\t :obligations-fn      register-free-names\n   529\t :parts-fn            (constantly nil)}\n   530\t```\n   531\t\n   532\tUnchanged from B6 section 5.2 in substance. Validation includes the\n   533\tlive-set rules; free names are `[:load-free rd name]` operands across all\n   534\tbodies. Loading is `yin.vm.debruijn.register/load-image`.\n   535\t\n   536\t### 5.5 Same-root pairing becomes derivation verification\n   537\t\n   538\tB6 section 7 paired H and R by mint-time datoms and verified the pair by\n   539\tre-lowering. With four formats the pair generalizes to the manifest's\n   540\tderivation records (section 8.1): one canonical tree, and one\n   541\tcontent-addressed record per format leading from that tree to the\n   542\tformat's identity. `trusted-fallback` and `verifying-fallback` keep their\n   543\tB6 names and shapes and read the derivation from the manifest; the\n   544\t`:pairing-mismatch` reason is retained as the name of a\n   545\t`:derivation-mismatch` raised during a fallback.\n   546\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
