{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '918,1066p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | nl -ba -v 918\"","aggregated_output":"   918\t## 8. The manifest registry\n   919\t\n   920\t### 8.1 The module manifest\n   921\t\n   922\tA manifest is content: one map, materialized in `dao.jing`, named by its\n   923\taddress. It replaces the `{sym fn}` dictionary entry.\n   924\t\n   925\t```clojure\n   926\t{:yin.module/name        'my.lib\n   927\t :yin.module/contract    \"v2\"\n   928\t :yin.module/tree        :segment/...        ; the one canonical tree\n   929\t :yin.module/derivations {:yin.semantic/code     :segment/...  ; record\n   930\t                          :yin.debruijn.code     :segment/...  ; record\n   931\t                          :yin.debruijn.register :segment/...} ; record\n   932\t :yin.module/index       {H :segment/... R :segment/...}       ; optional\n   933\t :yin.module/exports     #{'foo 'bar}\n   934\t :yin.module/requires    {'other.lib :segment/...}             ; manifest\n   935\t :yin.module/primitives  {'println :yin.k.pp/sha256-...}       ; profile\n   936\t :yin.module/footprint   {:store-keys #{} :effects #{}}}       ; UCF 7.6.1\n   937\t```\n   938\t\n   939\tRules:\n   940\t\n   941\t- **One tree.** `:yin.module/tree` is the root row id of the canonical\n   942\t  AST the module was authored as. The `:yin.ast/code` image *is* this\n   943\t  tree, so it has no derivation record.\n   944\t- **One derivation record per lowered format.** Each value under\n   945\t  `:yin.module/derivations` is the address of a content-addressed\n   946\t  derivation record in the shape `yin.vm.ledger/derive-record` mints:\n   947\t  `{:yin.ledger/op :derive :yin.ledger/input tree\n   948\t  :yin.ledger/output identity :yin.ledger/function f\n   949\t  :yin.ledger/profile {...}}`. The linker fetches the record (through a\n   950\t  `:yin.ledger/record` format record: `segment-matches?` identity, a\n   951\t  validator over these keys, no parts, no obligations) and checks\n   952\t  `:yin.ledger/input` equals `:yin.module/tree` and `:yin.ledger/output`\n   953\t  is the identity it then fetches. A record leading from a different\n   954\t  tree, or to a different identity, is `:derivation-mismatch`. Four\n   955\t  individually valid images from four different trees therefore cannot\n   956\t  share a manifest, and a swapped image fails before load.\n   957\t- **Verifying or trusting the derivation is composition policy.** With\n   958\t  `:fallback :verifying` (or whenever the composition asks), a linker\n   959\t  that implements the record's `:yin.ledger/profile` exactly re-lowers\n   960\t  the tree and compares the recomputed identity to `:yin.ledger/output`\n   961\t  (`yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` section 5.2.2, step 2); inequality is\n   962\t  `:derivation-mismatch`. A linker implementing a different profile does\n   963\t  not recompute; it reports the trust it extended as\n   964\t  `:trust :composition` in the outcome, exactly as B6's trusted fallback\n   965\t  did, and never silently.\n   966\t- **The name is verified.** Immediately after the manifest passes steps\n   967\t  2 to 4, the linker compares `:yin.module/name` with the\n   968\t  `:yin.link/name` it was resolved under; inequality is\n   969\t  `:module-name-mismatch` naming both. A name-environment entry can\n   970\t  therefore point only at a manifest that claims that name.\n   971\t- `:yin.module/index` maps contract-pinned identities to their storage\n   972\t  addresses, the H and R indexes of B6 section 6 carried beside the\n   973\t  identities they resolve. It is merged into linker-local `:indexes`\n   974\t  when the manifest is verified, never consulted from the wire.\n   975\t- `:yin.module/exports` are names, checked after the child evaluation\n   976\t  (section 7.3). `:yin.module/requires` maps each required module to the\n   977\t  manifest address the publisher linked against; `:yin.module/primitives`\n   978\t  maps each assumed host function to its profile address (UCF section\n   979\t  7.5.2). Together they are the declarations step 5a joins free names\n   980\t  with.\n   981\t- `:yin.module/footprint` is what `yin.vm.dependency-completion.md`\n   982\t  needs to report `:complete`; an undeclared footprint is `:incomplete`,\n   983\t  never a silent under-approximation.\n   984\t- The manifest is verified like any content: a `:yin.module/manifest`\n   985\t  format record with `:identity-matches-fn jing/segment-matches?`, a\n   986\t  validator over the keys above, no parts, no obligations.\n   987\t\n   988\t### 8.2 The name environment and its authority\n   989\t\n   990\tNames live outside the manifest. A name environment maps a module name\n   991\tto a manifest address and is linker-local state in one of two shapes:\n   992\t\n   993\t- a plain map `{'my.lib :segment/...}`, for tests and single-process\n   994\t  compositions, with the composition itself as the sole asserter;\n   995\t- assertions read from a `dao.space` source under the policy below.\n   996\t\n   997\t**Fail-closed assertion policy.** This policy is an entry criterion for\n   998\tM4: no linker may resolve a name from `dao.space` assertions before it is\n   999\timplemented and tested.\n  1000\t\n  1001\t- An assertion is the pair of datoms\n  1002\t  `[name :yin.module/manifest address]` and\n  1003\t  `[name :yin.module/asserted-by principal]` transacted together, where\n  1004\t  `principal` is a plain-data identity the composition recognizes. A\n  1005\t  manifest datom with no asserter datom in the same transaction is not\n  1006\t  an assertion and is ignored.\n  1007\t- The linker's `:authority` names the set of accepted principals and the\n  1008\t  **snapshot**: either a published index manifest address\n  1009\t  (`dao.space.index`) or a cursor position on the assertion stream. The\n  1010\t  linker reads exactly that snapshot; assertions appended afterwards do\n  1011\t  not exist for it until the composition advances the snapshot, which\n  1012\t  is an ordinary `link-state` rebuild, never an ambient re-read.\n  1013\t- At the snapshot, for one name: assertions by unaccepted principals are\n  1014\t  discarded; retractions are honored; the distinct manifest addresses\n  1015\t  remaining are counted. Exactly one resolves the name. Zero is\n  1016\t  `:absent`. More than one is `:ambiguous-name` naming every remaining\n  1017\t  address and asserter, and no address is chosen by recency, order, or\n  1018\t  any other rule.\n  1019\t- Provenance is data the outcome carries: a successful resolution names\n  1020\t  the asserter and the snapshot under `:yin.link/provenance` so a\n  1021\t  receiver can record which claim it acted on.\n  1022\t\n  1023\tAn entry is a claim. The manifest it names is verified, and its name is\n  1024\tverified against the entry (section 8.1). Who may be an accepted\n  1025\tprincipal, and how principals are authenticated, is the composition's\n  1026\tand is not answered here (section 12).\n  1027\t\n  1028\t### 8.3 What `yin.vm.module` becomes\n  1029\t\n  1030\tThe namespace keeps its shape and changes its contents.\n  1031\t\n  1032\t| Today                        | After                                       |\n  1033\t|------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|\n  1034\t| `register-module r name fns` | `register-host-module r name fns profiles`  |\n  1035\t|                              | (rules below); no code fetched, because the |\n  1036\t|                              | host is the boundary                        |\n  1037\t| `resolve-module r sym`       | unchanged signature; reads `:bindings`      |\n  1038\t| `require-handler`            | registry hit answers; installing joins the  |\n  1039\t|                              | waiter set; miss mints, parks, and emits    |\n  1040\t|                              | (section 7.2); never throws for absence     |\n  1041\t| `register-effect-handler`    | unchanged                                   |\n  1042\t| `stream-module`              | a host module; `register-stream-module`     |\n  1043\t|                              | calls `register-host-module`                |\n  1044\t| `default-registry`           | unchanged                                   |\n  1045\t| (new) `link-module r m d s`  | the `linked` transition of section 7.3      |\n  1046\t\n  1047\t**`register-host-module` enforces UCF profile classes.** Every binding\n  1048\tmust carry a profile in the shape of `yin.vm/primitive-profiles`, and\n  1049\tregistration refuses (throws, as a host assembly defect detected before\n  1050\tany operation runs) unless the profile's class is `:pure`, or\n  1051\t`:effectful` with a declared, non-empty `:yin.k/effects` set, and\n  1052\t`:yin.k/host-state` is `:none`. A `:host`-class function, a function\n  1053\twith undeclared host state, or a binding with no profile is refused. An\n  1054\t`:effectful` export must return plain effect data for the engine to\n  1055\tinterpret; it may not perform IO. `stream/make` is exactly such a pure\n  1056\teffect constructor, and the engine's `:make-stream` capability remains\n  1057\tthe explicit boundary that performs the creation. A host module is\n  1058\tentered as an already-linked manifest with `:yin.module/tree` absent,\n  1059\t`:yin.module/derivations {}`, and its exports listed under\n  1060\t`:yin.module/primitives` by profile address.\n  1061\t\n  1062\tThe registry value's `:modules` map changes from `{name {sym fn}}` to\n  1063\t`{name {:manifest m :address a :derivation d :bindings {sym value}}}`.\n  1064\tNo shim keeps the old entry shape: this is a dev-only repository with no\n  1065\tdeployed registries, and a clean break is the default here.\n  1066\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
