{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1067,1270p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md | nl -ba -v 1067\"","aggregated_output":"  1067\t## 9. Migration from `yin.vm.debruijn-linker`\n  1068\t\n  1069\tFive steps, each landing green on all three hosts before the next. The\n  1070\tpredecessor namespace is renamed, not aliased.\n  1071\t\n  1072\t```mermaid\n  1073\tflowchart TD\n  1074\t  M1[\"M1 rename\\nyin.vm.debruijn-linker -> yin.vm.linker\"]\n  1075\t  M2[\"M2 four format records\\nidentity-directed match, bounded parts\"]\n  1076\t  M3[\"M3 stepped core + link runtime\\nfetch = host policy; DHT behind server\"]\n  1077\t  M4[\"M4 require lowers to the linker\\nmanifests, authority, child install\"]\n  1078\t  M5[\"M5 yin.repl wires the four streams\\nper backend\"]\n  1079\t  M1 --> M2 --> M3 --> M4 --> M5\n  1080\t```\n  1081\t\n  1082\t**M1. Rename.** Move `src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc` to\n  1083\t`src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc` with namespace `yin.vm.linker`; move the\n  1084\ttest likewise. Update the five design documents that name the old\n  1085\tnamespace (`yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md`, `yin.vm.debruijn.register.md`,\n  1086\t`dao.agent.md`, `dao.agent.harness.md`, `dao.agent.mcp.server.md`) and\n  1087\tthe orchestrator log. Mark `yin.vm.debruijn.linker.md` as superseded by\n  1088\tthis document in its status line. No behavior changes. The B6 test\n  1089\tsuite passes unchanged apart from the require alias.\n  1090\t\n  1091\t**M2. Four format records.** Replace `:hash-fn` with `:identity-fn` and\n  1092\t`:identity-matches-fn`; rename `:free-names-fn` to `:obligations-fn`;\n  1093\tadd `:contract`, `:row-defect-fn`, and `:parts-fn`; add `ast-format`,\n  1094\t`semantic-format`, `semantic-free-names`, and `row-local-defect`. Make\n  1095\tstep 2 the bounded worklist. `yin.vm.content` keeps `materialize-tree!`\n  1096\tand `materialize-vector!` as the mint side (they are `publish!` for those\n  1097\tformats); `load-rows` and `fetch-vector` are retired, and their callers\n  1098\tmove to `fetch` with the new records. Tests, beyond B6's matrix for the\n  1099\ttwo new formats: a tree with one absent child row is `:absent` naming\n  1100\tthat row; a tree with one corrupt child row is `:address-mismatch`\n  1101\tnaming it; a tree whose root is well-formed but whose child has a bad\n  1102\ttag is `:descriptor-defect` with no fetch of that child's slots; a tree\n  1103\texceeding `:max-parts` is `:parts-limit`; a vector whose index entry\n  1104\tpoints at a different valid vector is `:hash-mismatch`; a vector minted\n  1105\tunder `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n  1106\t`:blake3`.\n  1107\t\n  1108\t**M3. Stepped core and link runtime.** Implement `link-state`,\n  1109\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon` over `dao.jing.remote.step` (or, for a\n  1110\tpurely local composition, over `dao.stream.rpc` on a ring-buffer pair\n  1111\tserved by `dao.jing.remote/serve-content!`'s handlers). Reimplement\n  1112\t`fetch` as the blocking driver over a link runtime; export `verify` and\n  1113\t`discharge`. Tests: the full refusal matrix through `step` over ring\n  1114\tbuffers on all three hosts; the JVM WebSocket path from B6 completion\n  1115\tcriterion 1; a `:pending` sequence where the content server answers one\n  1116\tpart per step; a request carrying a function or a handle is\n  1117\t`:invalid-request`; the local-fetch traffic test of section 6.4 with a\n  1118\t`get`-counting server handle and a handle-free linker state; the DHT\n  1119\thandle behind `serve-content!` answering a link over ring buffers with\n  1120\tthe server driven by the test.\n  1121\t\n  1122\t**M4. `require` lowers to the linker.** Entry criterion: the section 8.2\n  1123\tassertion policy is implemented and its tests pass (accepted and\n  1124\tunaccepted asserters, retraction, two accepted assertions refusing\n  1125\t`:ambiguous-name`, snapshot advance). Then: the manifest and derivation\n  1126\tformat records; `register-host-module` with profile enforcement;\n  1127\t`require-handler` minting, parking, and emitting; the two wait states\n  1128\tthrough `check-wait-set` with id correlation; the install child in the\n  1129\tscheduler with the section 7.3 phases; `link-module`; the UCF table\n  1130\tamendments. Tests, per backend: a require of an unlinked module over\n  1131\tring buffers completes and the program resumes with its exports bound;\n  1132\ta manifest declaring a different name is `:module-name-mismatch`; a\n  1133\tmanifest whose semantic, H, or R derivation leads from a different tree\n  1134\tis `:derivation-mismatch` (three swapped-image tests, and a fourth\n  1135\twhere the `:yin.ast/code` tree is not the manifest's tree); a\n  1136\tsame-named primitive of different profile at the receiver is\n  1137\t`:unresolved-free`; a shadowed export name in the requiring program's\n  1138\tstore is `:shadowed-free`; a free name the manifest never declares is\n  1139\t`:undeclared-free`; two outstanding requires on one response stream\n  1140\teach restore on their own id; a response landing before the entry would\n  1141\thave been polled is not skipped; a module requiring another links\n  1142\ttransitively while a third task keeps running; a require cycle is\n  1143\t`:require-cycle`; `(vm :stack)` and `(vm :register)` in `yin.repl` link\n  1144\tthe same manifest by H and R respectively and produce B0-equal results.\n  1145\t\n  1146\t**M5. `yin.repl` wiring.** The REPL composes the link pair per VM and\n  1147\tthe content pair per connection (`connect` already opens the RPC\n  1148\tclient). `(require 'foo)` at the prompt exercises the whole path.\n  1149\t\n  1150\tCoexistence during M4: host modules are entered by\n  1151\t`register-host-module` from the first commit of M4, so every existing\n  1152\tcomposition keeps working while linked modules are added. There is no\n  1153\tperiod in which two registry shapes coexist.\n  1154\t\n  1155\t## 10. File box\n  1156\t\n  1157\t```text\n  1158\tRenamed:  src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_linker.cljc\n  1159\t            -> src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc            (M1)\n  1160\t          test/yin/vm/debruijn_linker_test.cljc\n  1161\t            -> test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc           (M1)\n  1162\tNew:      test/yin/vm/linker_step_test.cljc           (M3)\n  1163\t          test/yin/vm/linker_authority_test.cljc      (M4 entry)\n  1164\t          test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc        (M4)\n  1165\tEdited:   src/cljc/yin/vm/module.cljc                 (M4)\n  1166\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc  (:link-request, :link-response,\n  1167\t                                        :install wait reasons; the\n  1168\t                                        install child)             (M4)\n  1169\t          src/cljc/yin/vm/content.cljc (retire load-rows,\n  1170\t                                        fetch-vector)              (M2)\n  1171\t          src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc                      (M5)\n  1172\t          docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\n  1173\t            (section 7.4.1 rows, section 7.4.3 variants)           (M4)\n  1174\tDepends:  dao.jing (segment-key, segment-matches?, materialize!)\n  1175\t          dao.jing.remote, dao.jing.remote.step, dao.stream.rpc\n  1176\t          yin.vm (validate-rows, free-names, primitive-profiles)\n  1177\t          yin.vm.code (well-formed-vector?)\n  1178\t          yin.vm.ledger (derive-record, verify-derivation)\n  1179\t          yin.vm.debruijn-code, yin.vm.debruijn-register-code\n  1180\tMust not change:\n  1181\t          image-hash, register-hash, segment-key, the opcode\n  1182\t          tables, dao.stream, dao.jing, any kernel's step function\n  1183\t```\n  1184\t\n  1185\t`yin.vm.linker` exports: `fetch`, `verify`, `discharge`, `link-state`,\n  1186\t`request-link`, `step`, `abandon`, `publish!`, `ast-format`,\n  1187\t`semantic-format`, `stack-format`, `register-format`, `manifest-format`,\n  1188\t`record-format`, the four free-name scanners, `row-local-defect`,\n  1189\t`index-from-datoms`, `address-attribute`, `trusted-fallback`,\n  1190\t`verifying-fallback`, `refused`, `refused?`, `ok?`, `refusal-reasons`.\n  1191\t\n  1192\t## 11. Completion criteria\n  1193\t\n  1194\tStructure:\n  1195\t\n  1196\t1. One `fetch` and one `step` serve all four formats with no\n  1197\t   format-specific branching; a fifth format is one record.\n  1198\t2. No global loader, registry, callback, or cache; every input is an\n  1199\t   argument or VM-state value; no function or handle ever appears in a\n  1200\t   value on the link or content streams.\n  1201\t3. Tri-host parity (JVM, Node, ClojureDart), 0 kondo errors, clean\n  1202\t   cljstyle.\n  1203\t4. This file and `yin.vm.linker` are pure ASCII with every line at most\n  1204\t   80 columns.\n  1205\t\n  1206\tVerification:\n  1207\t\n  1208\t5. Every B6 completion criterion (section 11 there) holds for all four\n  1209\t   formats where applicable, through both `fetch` and `step`.\n  1210\t6. A payload whose address is valid but whose identity is not the one\n  1211\t   requested is refused for every format, including the two whose\n  1212\t   identity is a storage address, and under every registered algorithm.\n  1213\t7. A request naming a contract the format record does not implement is\n  1214\t   `:contract-mismatch` before validation runs.\n  1215\t8. A malformed row is refused before any of its children is requested,\n  1216\t   and every composition bound produces `:parts-limit`.\n  1217\t9. Local `fetch` produces exactly the content-pair traffic the stepped\n  1218\t   path produces and holds no content handle.\n  1219\t\n  1220\tRequire:\n  1221\t\n  1222\t10. `(require 'foo)` on each of the four backends, over ring buffers,\n  1223\t    parks, links, installs through the child phases, and resumes with\n  1224\t    `'foo`; the same over the JVM WebSocket content path.\n  1225\t11. The registry value holds no function that arrived by linking; every\n  1226\t    linked module's `:bindings` came from an isolated child evaluation\n  1227\t    that reached halt with every export bound.\n  1228\t12. UCF section 7.4.1 carries `:link-request`, `:link-response`, and\n  1229\t    `:install` safepoints, section 7.4.3 their pending variants, and a\n  1230\t    parked entry of each kind lifts and lowers through UCF's round-trip\n  1231\t    test.\n  1232\t13. Every swapped-image and swapped-name case in M4 refuses before load.\n  1233\t14. The assertion policy of section 8.2 refuses `:ambiguous-name` and\n  1234\t    ignores unaccepted asserters, at a fixed snapshot.\n  1235\t\n  1236\t## 12. Open decisions\n  1237\t\n  1238\tRecorded so a later plan does not rediscover them. None blocks M1 to M3;\n  1239\tthe first is an M4 entry criterion in its policy half and open only in\n  1240\tits authentication half.\n  1241\t\n  1242\t- **Principal authentication.** Section 8.2 fixes what the linker does\n  1243\t  with assertions from accepted and unaccepted principals. How a\n  1244\t  principal proves it is who the asserter datom says is not fixed:\n  1245\t  signed assertions, a capability token, or composition trust are all\n  1246\t  compatible with the policy, and `dao.stream.md` records that\n  1247\t  self-certifying identities live in the payload, above the stream.\n  1248\t- **SCC identity.** B7 hashes a mutually recursive component as one unit\n  1249\t  with canonical member ordering. Whether that unit is a manifest of\n  1250\t  manifests or a single image per format is undecided; section 7.4\n  1251\t  fixes only the response shape and the cycle refusal.\n  1252\t- **Failure policy.** Retry, deadline, and permanent absence for a\n  1253\t  `:pending` link are the composition's (D6). Whether `yin.repl` adopts\n  1254\t  the `dao.jing.remote` timing options or its own is an M5 decision.\n  1255\t- **Contract-pinned AST and semantic identities.** Strict decoupling of\n  1256\t  storage address from VM identity holds for H and R only (section 3).\n  1257\t  Pinning `:yin.ast/code` and `:yin.semantic/code` identities to a\n  1258\t  contract hash, with explicit identity-to-address indexes, is an\n  1259\t  amendment to UCF section 7.3.2 and `yin.vm.code-as-tuples.md` section\n  1260\t  4.1. The linker is prepared for it: `:identity-matches-fn` and\n  1261\t  `:indexes` are the only slots that would change.\n  1262\t- **A stepped DHT client.** The DHT is served behind the content\n  1263\t  boundary (section 6.1). A portable, non-blocking DHT client that could\n  1264\t  sit on the linker's side is a `dao.jing.dht` design.\n  1265\t- **Unrecognized outcomes.** `dao.stream.md` OD-1 proposes that a\n  1266\t  consumer treat an unrecognized outcome as refused and not retryable.\n  1267\t  The stepped core follows that rule once OD-1 is accepted; until then\n  1268\t  it classifies unknown content-server answers as `transport-error`, as\n  1269\t  `dao.stream.observe/step` does.\n  1270\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
